## Findings

**Note on path:** `node_modules/commerce-sdk-isomorphic/dist/` does not exist in this install (v5.2.0) — `package.json` (`main`/`module`) points to `lib/`, not `dist/`. AGENTS.md's citation is stale. I used `lib/index.esm.d.ts` (byte-identical to `lib/index.cjs.d.ts`).

### 1. Type-level evidence

`ShopperProductsModelTypes.Inventory` — `node_modules/commerce-sdk-isomorphic/lib/index.esm.d.ts:59675-59685`:
```ts
type Inventory = {
    ats?: number;
    backorderable?: boolean;
    id: string;
    inStockDate?: string;
    orderable?: boolean;
    preorderable?: boolean;
    stockLevel?: number;
} & { [key: string]: any; };
```
`Product` (line 59783) has `inventory?: Inventory` (59792), `inventories?: Array<Inventory>` (59791), `variants?: Array<Variant>` (59826). `ShopperProductsModelTypes.Variant` (59538) only has `orderable?: boolean` — no stock fields of its own.

`ShopperSearchModelTypes.ProductSearchHit` (line 63919) has a flat `orderable?: boolean` (63923) and `variants?: Array<Variant>` (63936, search-scoped `Variant` at 63809 also just `orderable?: boolean`) — but **no `inventory`/`inventories` field at all**. The search/tile-facing type is strictly less detailed than the full `Product` type.

### 2. Real precedent

`node_modules/@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/hooks/use-derived-product.js:37,72-78`:
```js
const stockLevel = product?.inventory?.stockLevel || 0
...
const isOutOfStock =
    !stockLevel ||
    (!isProductABundle && !variant && !isStandardProduct &&
        Object.keys(variationParams).length === variationAttributes.length) ||
    (!isProductABundle && variant && !variant.orderable)
```
Also `app/components/product-view/index.jsx:146-151` (`validateOrderability`): `(variant?.orderable || product?.inventory?.orderable) && quantity > 0 && quantity <= stockLevel`.

**Negative finding**: the base `product-tile/index.jsx` (closest analog to `ZimmProductCard`) has **zero** orderable/inventory logic — it only reads `product.type.{set,bundle,item}` and custom badge flags `c_isNew`/`c_isSale` (`app/constants.js:52-69`). There is no existing tile-level "unavailable" precedent; the only real derivation lives in the PDP hook, which needs the full `Product` shape (`.inventory`), not `ProductSearchHit`.

### 3. Edge cases (evidence-based, not speculative)

Variant rollup — `app/hooks/use-variation-attributes.js:74-82`:
```js
export const isVariantValueOrderable = (product, variationParams) => {
    return product.variants
        .filter(({variationValues}) => Object.keys(variationParams).every(
            (key) => variationValues[key] === variationParams[key]))
        .some(({orderable}) => orderable)
}
```
Confirms per-size availability is real and handled by filtering matching variants, not a single flag.

Basket-level "unavailable" — `app/components/unavailable-product-confirmation-modal/index.jsx:67-74`: unavailable = product missing from `getProducts` response, OR `!inventory.orderable`, OR orderable-but-`quantity > stockLevel`.

Preorder/backorder: `backorderable`/`preorderable`/`inStockDate`/`ats` exist in the type, but a full-tree grep shows these four fields appear **only** in mock/test fixtures (e.g. `app/mocks/mock-data.js:2227-2231`) — zero production code reads them. Statically, the base app always collapses to `orderable`/`stockLevel`; whether live SFCC data needs finer preorder/backorder UI can't be confirmed from static code alone.
